# Router driver rules

- All modem models implement `RouterDriver` from `src/core/router/types.ts`.
- Register new models in `src/core/router/index.ts`.
- Keep CGI/OID strings and response parsing inside the model folder (e.g. `vx220/`).
- Use `routerHttp` / `clearRouterSession` from `src/core/router/http.ts` for I/O.
- Do not call `fetch` directly to the modem from the UI layer.
- Treat firmware differences as driver concerns; keep UI model-agnostic.
- When adding write operations (block, QoS), implement read/list first and gate writes behind explicit user actions.
- Parse responses with shared helpers when possible; avoid brittle full-string matches.
